'''Companyia de Productes Químics Pesants Balboa, S.A.''' ({{lang|ca|Companyia de Productes Químics Pesants Balboa}}), commonly abbreviated '''PQQB''', is a Balboan {{w|specialty chemicals}} company headquartered in [[Portnou]]. The company manufactures refrigerants, soaps, industrial solvents, base chemicals for cosmetics, and selected fertilizers. It is one of the main chemical producers in the Portnou industrial zone and supplies both domestic Balboan customers and export markets across the [[BTPMEU]] region.

PQQB is listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] and is a constituent of the [[SCX 100]] index. Its headquarters are in Portnou, while its main campus is in [[Badia Curta]], giving it access to port infrastructure, refinery-linked feedstocks, and distribution routes.

== History ==

=== Founding (1991) ===

PQQB was established in 1991 as a Portnou-based industrial chemicals producer by the [[Consorci Portnou]], a local consortium formed to develop heavy chemical manufacturing in the canal terminus region. The company was intended to supply downstream chemical products to Balboa's manufacturing, consumer goods, and agricultural sectors while making use of Portnou's transport advantages.

The initial production slate focused on industrial solvents and soap intermediates, with refrigerants added soon after as the company expanded its chlorinated and fluorinated chemical capacity. The company also developed a line of base chemicals used in cosmetic formulations, including surfactants, emulsifiers, and fatty alcohol derivatives.

=== Expansion ===

During the 2000s and 2010s, PQQB expanded its product range into fertilizers and broader specialty chemical intermediates. Its fertilizer output remained smaller than that of the major agricultural chemical producers, but it became an established supplier of blended and value-added products for Balboa's domestic market.

The company's growth was supported by Portnou's role as a logistics hub for canal traffic and warehousing. The Badia Curta campus linked PQQB to refinery-linked feedstocks, while proximity to the Balboa Canal and Sant Cristòfor shipping networks gave the company an advantage in importing inputs and exporting finished goods.

== Products ==

PQQB's product portfolio includes:

* '''Refrigerants''': Industrial and commercial refrigerant gases and blends.
* '''Soaps''': Industrial, household, and institutional soap bases.
* '''Industrial solvents''': General-purpose solvents and formulation additives.
* '''Cosmetic base chemicals''': Base ingredients for creams, lotions, cleansers, and personal-care products.
* '''Fertilizers''': Selected nitrogenous and blended fertilizer products.
* '''Surfactants''': Detergent intermediates and specialty surfactants.

== Operations ==

* '''Headquarters''': [[Portnou]], [[Balboa]]
* '''Main complex''': Portnou industrial zone — chemical synthesis, blending, packaging, and bulk storage facilities
* '''Employees''': approximately 4,100 (2026)

PQQB's operations are concentrated in Portnou, where it maintains synthesis units, blending lines, packaging facilities, and storage terminals. The company uses Portnou's position at the canal terminus to distribute products by rail, road, and ship to domestic and export markets.

== Ownership ==

PQQB is publicly traded on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] but remains anchored by the Portnou industrial consortium:

* '''[[Consorci Portnou]]''': 48% — majority owner and industrial sponsor
* '''[[Fons d'Inversió Directa de Balboa]] (FIDB)''': 7% — domestic institutional holding
* '''[[Balboa Pension Fund]] (BPF)''': 5% — domestic institutional holding
* '''Public float''': approximately 40% — held by institutional and retail investors

== Competition ==

PQQB competes with several Balboan chemical producers. In solvents and industrial formulations, it competes with [[Corporació Nacional de Fabricants de Solvents]] and [[Companyia Química Occidental]]. In fertilizers, it competes with [[Nutrició del Món]]. In soaps and cosmetic base chemicals, it competes with smaller domestic formulators and importers, while also supplying intermediates to consumer-goods companies.

The company is generally positioned as a mid-sized diversified chemical producer with strong logistics access rather than as a pure specialty player.

